Freenpipe local change to audiopipe (applied by third_party/vendor.sh).

Let the caller choose the ONNX Runtime execution provider of the Parakeet
engine. `Model::from_pretrained_cache_only_with`,
`ParakeetEngine::from_pretrained_cache_only_with` and
`ParakeetEngine::from_dir_with` take an `Accelerator`: `Auto` keeps the
existing behaviour (DirectML only when SCREENPIPE_DIRECTML=1/true, silent CPU
fallback), `Cpu` forces the CPU provider, and `DirectMl { device_id }` builds
DirectML sessions on that DXGI adapter with memory patterns and parallel
execution off, returning an error when the provider cannot be registered.
Freenpipe's screenpipe-audio (transcription/parakeet_windows.rs) picks the
adapter, honours SCREENPIPE_DIRECTML and handles recycling and CPU recovery.
The existing functions keep their signatures and behaviour.

